{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms","id":1380094,"title":"How Good are DB Charms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-10T05:57:12-07:00","id":1380094,"title":"How Good are DB Charms?","content":"Hello, I have a question and I think it's going to require a lot of words, so I thought it was better to ask in a new topic instead of bloating the Ask a Question one.<br /> <br /> Also, if I can, I'd like to summon <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a> for this, since I read his analysis of both the Lunar and DB splats (yes, I'm a filthy lurker).<br /> <br /> So, in the already mentioned analysis, it turned out that DB sucks majorly against both Lunar and Solar Exalted. That's to be expected, of course, since they have clear weaknesses, especially regarding their Excellencies and their mote pool. Having both less fuel in their tanks and a dice pool maximum inferior to their opponents limit them a lot. Their Charms are also inferior and interact with their Aura in complicated ways. I'm absolutely terrible at remembering what Charms do because dice adders -that are not Excellencies-, dice tricks, and similar things are just white noise for me. The Charms I remember better are the ones that have some strange, esoteric effect, like most Charms that have clear visual effects. But even I can see that Aura is a little clunky at times.<br /> <br /> But how good are their Charms without all those problems? What if the DB had the same -or comparable- Motes of the Solar and Lunar, their Excellency let them have a similar dice pools (in the range of 21, plus whatever for weapons) and the Aura mechanic was a little easier (like, your Aura count as both your Aspect element and the one you used to increase your anima). <br /> <br /> How would DB compare to Solar and Lunars in that case? How good their Charms would be if they had Celestial level mote pool and Excellencies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T07:41:11-07:00","id":1380111,"title":"","content":"I don't understand the question.<br /> <br /> Solar Charms &gt; Mastery Martial Arts &gt; Lunar Charms &gt; Martial Arts &amp; DB Charms in Aura &gt; Dragon-Blooded Charms out of Aura &gt; Terrestrial Martial Arts<br /> <br /> An optimized DB (RAW) can easily take down an &quot;average&quot; Celestial. An optimized Celestial can easily take down 2(-ish) optimized DBs.<br /> <br /> If DBs had 21 dice caps, easy aura, more motes... they'd be much more powerful. But I still don't understand the question.<br /> <br /> The Essence 5 Solar Medicine capstone is Perfect Celestial Chirurgeon: double 7s on a Medicine roll, 1/story.<br /> The Essence 5 DB Medicine capstone is Most Beneficent Seed of the Five Dragons: double 7s on a Medicine roll, 1/story <i>for 5m 1ahl</i> but with a reset condition.<br /> <br /> A Solar can start with their capstone Charm. A DB can't. The DB can reset their Charm. A Solar can't. The Solar Charm is FREE. The DB Charm will flare if Peripheral Essence is used, and costs an Aggrevated health level. Solars have a 21 dice cap for 10m (Ave. 16 successes; 10+ successes 95% of the time). DBs have a 17 dice cap with a free non-Charm success for 6m (Ave. 15 successes; 9+ successes 95% of the time) for 6m. A Solar pays +4m for +1 success. Rules As Written.<br /> <br /> These metrics don't change if you give the DB more motes and free Wood Aura. But 21 dice with double-7s and a free success (Ave. 17 successes; 11+ successes 95% of the time) is better than 17 dice with double-7s and a free success.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded are the weakest of the Exalted... but as the Exalted they are still really good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-11-2020, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T07:54:23-07:00","id":1380115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1380111#post1380111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, excluding everything else, how DB charms compare to Celestial Charms?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1380111#post1380111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Essence 5 Solar Medicine capstone is Perfect Celestial Chirurgeon: double 7s on a medicine roll, 1/story.<br /> The Essence 5 DB Medicine capstone is Most Beneficent Seed of the Five Dragons: double 7s on a Medicine roll, 1/story <i>for 5m 1ahl</i> but with a reset condition.<br /> <br /> A Solar can start with their capstone Charm. A DB can't. The DB can reset their Charm. A Solar can't. The Solar Charm is FREE. The DB Charm will flare if peripheral, and costs an Aggrevated health level. Solars have a 20 dice cap for 10m. DBs have a 17 dice cap with a free non-Charm success for 6m.<br /> <br /> These metrics don't change if you give the DB more motes and free Wood Aura. But 21 dice with double-7s and a free success is better than 17 dice with double-7s and a free success.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I wanted to see. As I said, I'm terrible with Charms, but from this, I understand that, given the obvious difference in dices, the DB Charm is pretty comparable to the Solar one, but it costs more. <br /> <br /> Is that something that's true for all DB Charms, or you just a coincidence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T08:04:18-07:00","id":1380118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1380115#post1380115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I wanted to see. As I said, I'm terrible with Charms, but from this, I understand that, given the obvious difference in dices, the DB Charm is pretty comparable to the Solar one, but it costs more.<br /> <br /> Is that something that's true for all DB Charms, or you just a coincidence?</div> </div> </div> </div>Many DB Charms are either much weaker or much more expensive than their Celestial counterparts. A DB needs to be <b>Essence </b>3 to learn a Charm which, for <b>4m</b>, grants <b>double 9s</b> on investigation rolls... against Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Edit: </i>DB Charms that can compare with Celestial Charms are usually limited by Aura mechanics. If your goal is to get DBs to the Celestial level, then slightly better Auras isn't gonna cut it, you'll need to bypass aura requirements altogether. If you wanna keep aura for flavor you could always say that expending an Aura you don't have costs 1wp or something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 04-10-2020, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T09:55:49-07:00","id":1380151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1380115#post1380115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, excluding everything else, how DB charms compare to Celestial Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, still don't understand the question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's what I wanted to see. As I said, I'm terrible with Charms, but from this, I understand that, given the obvious difference in dices, the DB Charm is pretty comparable to the Solar one, but it costs more. <br /> <br /> Is that something that's true for all DB Charms, or you just a coincidence? </div> </div> </div>Ehhhh... not all Charms.<br /> <br /> Highlights<br /> <br /> Archery<br /> Solar: Phantom Arrow Technique (starting Charm), fire your bow for 1m instead of using arrows. Reflexive. 1/scene get bonus attack dice based on an Intimacy at the cost of &quot;spending&quot; that Intimacy. May make one arrow indestructible at Essence 3. <br /> DB: Harvest of the Hunter (starting Charm), get guaranteed arrows on a successful ammunition check, with double-8s. Supplemental. 1m.<br /> <br /> Both Solars and DBs can keep firing their bow once they run out of arrows. Ammunition checks are Reflexive, scavenging is an action. Solars are spending 1m every turn for guaranteed success. DBs are spending 1m every five turns with a chance if failure. Solars get bonus powers tacked onto their Charm. DBs can fully replenish their arrows (which means they can share with their allies). Solars more powerful but costlier, DBs more efficient.<br /> <br /> Athletics<br /> Solars: Increasing Strength Exercise. Simple. 3m, +1 Strength/scene. Stackable upto the lower of (Essence times) or (double Strength). Bonus Decisive damage. May pay with Initiative instead of motes.<br /> DB: Strength of Stone Technique. Simple. 5m, +1 Strength/scene. Must be standing on the ground. <s>Bonus Withering damage.</s><br /> <br /> <s>The bonus damage is a wash.</s> The DB Charm is more expensive (to the point of raising your Anima), not stackable, and has conditions on its use. Honestly there's not much in it. You are usually standing on the ground. +2m isn't a massive deal. <s>You are really unlikey to be in a position where you can just stand still and charge up Increasing Strength Exercise five times in a row.</s> But the Solar Charm is clearly better.<br /> <br /> Awareness<br /> Solar: Awakening Eye (Essence 1). 5m 1WP. Get a free full Excellency to Join Battle, with extra non-Charm dice, and bonus successes to find hidden enemies.<br /> DB: One-With-Earth Embodiment (Essence 3, Signature). 10m 1WP. Swim through earth (including stone) like water.<br /> <br /> DB Charms do not always work anything like Solar Charms. If you're really good at feeling vibrations, DBs can swim through solid stone and Solars can go first in combat. Solar Charms represent things humans can do dialled up to 11. DB Charms are about manipulating the elements.<br /> <br /> Brawl<br /> Solars: Excellent Brawl (free Charm). Gain upto +10d for 1m each.<br /> DB: Become the Hammer (Excellency). Gain upto +6d for 1m each. Parry lethal damage unarmed. Reroll 6s on damage.<br /> <br /> The Solar Charm has more raw power, but the DB Charm has WAAAAY loads more utility.<br /> <br /> Bureaucracy<br /> Solar: Soul-Snaring Pitch (Essence 3). Make any deal, no matter how bad it is, automatically with anyone who has a lower Willpower than your Essence score or with massive bonuses to the roll if their Willpower is higher.<br /> DB: Distraction of the Babbling Brook (Essence 3, Signature). Sneak a hidden clause into a deal, taking a penalty based on how severe it is. 1/story.<br /> <br /> The Solar charm is stronger, easier to use, and not limited to once per Story. It's much better. But both Solars and DBs can convince you to sell yourself into slavery.<br /> <br /> Craft<br /> Solar: Craftsman Needs No Tools (Essence 1). 6m. Drastically speed up Major and Basic projects for all Crafts, and work without tools.<br /> DB: Stone-Carving Fingers AND Shaping Hand Style (Essence 2). 6m. Speed up Major and Basic projects OR work without tools, so long as you either work stone or a Craft you have at 4-dots or more.<br /> <br /> What takes DBs 2 Charms and Essence 2, Solars do at Essence 1 with 1 Charm. And Solars are more powerful. And Solars are more versatile. <br /> <br /> Dodge<br /> Solar: Shadow Dancer Method. Spend 1m to not lose Initiative on a Disengage. Gain Initiative whenever you Disengage then move back in.<br /> DB: Heat-of-Battle Advance. Spend 2m to not lose Initiative on a Disengage AND get extra dice on the attempt, but can only use it if moving towards an enemy, and the Charm is Perilous.<br /> <br /> The Solar Charm is cheaper, easier to use, and directly helps you win combats. The DB Charm is more powerful, but is more expensive and of more limited use.<br /> <br /> Hopefully that's illustrative.<br /> <br /> (There's an Essence 3 Solar Investigation Charm which gives you 3 <i>Charm</i> successes for 6m. Basically giving you a Muted, no discount Excellency. They also have Shadow Over Day, which is &quot;buy a Charm to save 1m under extremely limited circumstances... maybe&quot;. So it's not like it's just DBs who have bad Charms.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-11-2020, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T10:05:28-07:00","id":1380152,"title":"","content":"One other thing you\u2019d want to do is make more DB charms Supplemental instead of Simple. One of a Solar\u2019s really powerful abilities, on top of dice cap, good charms and Supernal, is their ability to combine ten different powerful charms at once, and even on reflexive actions. For example Thunderbolt Attack Prana, it doubles decisive damage. Roaring River Slash also doubles damage, but being a simple charm or can\u2019t be combined with other simple charms or reflexive actions like TAP can. Although TAP also has the restriction that it must be used on a target a range band away.<br /> <br /> A lot of direct DB charm effects though only end up being weaker when they\u2019re straight power abilities too. For example Fire and Stones Strike if you\u2019re Strength 5 it\u2019s 5 motes for 5 damage, for a DB it\u2019s 3m 1wp for 5 damage using Crimson Fang Bite, similar effect but greater cost. On the other hand something like Flowing God Dragon Stance is a DB charm that turns your body into water for the scene for 15m 1wp letting you slip through cracks in the floor, keyholes, underneath doors, also granting +1 evasion and Essence/2 bonus successes which are non-charm while in water. Solars just don\u2019t get anything like that, because \u201cturn your body into liquid.\u201d Is waaaay outside of Solar power. The closest they get is a 10m 1wp charm that lets them pass immaterially through one locked door or grate, the only benefit is that it works on waterproof portals. <br /> <br /> So basically DB charms are harder to combo together, usually cost more, although their effects are often pretty close to as good, and in some specific cases even better where their mastery of elements applies. Also some effects that are almost incomparable like lighting a brushfire around you while you rush an enemy, or using awareness charms to destroy an enemy\u2019s motes of essence. Unique effects that are like nothing Solars can do.<br /> <br /> I would also give some caution against trying to equalize the two outside of very specific games. One of the things that makes Solars cool is the awesome feats they can perform. If a DB could perform those same awesome feats as well as all the cool elemental powers they have the Solars aren\u2019t really left with much. Also Solars are on the unquestioned top dogs for mechanical power and unquestioned bottom dogs for everything else. Playing a Solar is supposed to feel great because you\u2019re so strong, and also confining because you have to hide that power whenever you can, DB games feel great because you can totally cut loose and abuse the fact that most populations believe you to be living saints, while being not so powerful that you can just punch through any problem you come across. In mixed games it could even be an issue \u201cSo this Fire aspect guy is just as badass in combat as me, and can flare his anima in public, and get his way with almost anyone by saying \u2018doing this for me would give YOU the gratitude of House Cathak.\u2019 So why am I playing a Solar again?\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T11:08:43-07:00","id":1380159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1380152#post1380152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One other thing you\u2019d want to do is make more DB charms Supplemental instead of Simple. One of a Solar\u2019s really powerful abilities, on top of dice cap, good charms and Supernal, is their ability to combine ten different powerful charms at once, and even on reflexive actions. For example Thunderbolt Attack Prana, it doubles decisive damage. Roaring River Slash also doubles damage, but being a simple charm or can\u2019t be combined with other simple charms or reflexive actions like TAP can. Although TAP also has the restriction that it must be used on a target a range band away.<br /> <br /> A lot of direct DB charm effects though only end up being weaker when they\u2019re straight power abilities too. For example Fire and Stones Strike if you\u2019re Strength 5 it\u2019s 5 motes for 5 damage, for a DB it\u2019s 3m 1wp for 5 damage using Crimson Fang Bite, similar effect but greater cost. On the other hand something like Flowing God Dragon Stance is a DB charm that turns your body into water for the scene for 15m 1wp letting you slip through cracks in the floor, keyholes, underneath doors, also granting +1 evasion and Essence/2 bonus successes which are non-charm while in water. Solars just don\u2019t get anything like that, because \u201cturn your body into liquid.\u201d Is waaaay outside of Solar power. The closest they get is a 10m 1wp charm that lets them pass immaterially through one locked door or grate, the only benefit is that it works on waterproof portals.<br /> <br /> So basically DB charms are harder to combo together, usually cost more, although their effects are often pretty close to as good, and in some specific cases even better where their mastery of elements applies. Also some effects that are almost incomparable like lighting a brushfire around you while you rush an enemy, or using awareness charms to destroy an enemy\u2019s motes of essence. Unique effects that are like nothing Solars can do.<br /> <br /> <b>I would also give some caution against trying to equalize the two outside of very specific games.</b> One of the things that makes Solars cool is the awesome feats they can perform. If a DB could perform those same awesome feats as well as all the cool elemental powers they have the Solars aren\u2019t really left with much. Also Solars are on the unquestioned top dogs for mechanical power and unquestioned bottom dogs for everything else. Playing a Solar is supposed to feel great because you\u2019re so strong, and also confining because you have to hide that power whenever you can, DB games feel great because you can totally cut loose and abuse the fact that most populations believe you to be living saints, while being not so powerful that you can just punch through any problem you come across. In mixed games it could even be an issue \u201cSo this Fire aspect guy is just as badass in combat as me, and can flare his anima in public, and get his way with almost anyone by saying \u2018doing this for me would give YOU the gratitude of House Cathak.\u2019 So why am I playing a Solar again?\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, I was just curious to know if increasing the dicepools and the motes of the DB made them too good for what they're supposed to be in the setting, but from the answers I get there, it doesn't seems like it does. Even with more or less equal dices, the DB seems to have a clear disadvantage on Celestial Exalted, unless we're talking of specific Charms.<br /> <br /> Which is cool. It make -relatively- easier to power them up without making them Elemental Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T11:39:19-07:00","id":1380166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shapechanger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1380159#post1380159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no, I was just curious to know if increasing the dicepools and the motes of the DB made them too good for what they're supposed to be in the setting, but from the answers I get there, it doesn't seems like it does. Even with more or less equal dices, the DB seems to have a clear disadvantage on Celestial Exalted, unless we're talking of specific Charms.<br /> <br /> Which is cool. It make -relatively- easier to power them up without making them Elemental Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, now I understand.<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Charms are weaker than Celestial Charms. There's room to power them up and not be better than Solars, but they're balanced around where they are now. Like my Medicine example where your power-up makes the DB Charm stronger than the Solar one, and resettable (albeit at a higher cost).<br /> <br /> If you wanted to up the opposition for powerful Celestial's, I'd encourage you to just cheat. QCs don't use the same powers as PCs mechanically.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to power up your Deeb PCs in a Deeb game, then pretty much just go for it.<br /> <br /> If you have a mixed splat game... just embrace the power difference. That's literally the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-10-2020, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T14:50:39-07:00","id":1380208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1380151#post1380151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Athletics<br /> Solars: Increasing Strength Exercise. Simple. 3m, +1 Strength/scene. Stackable upto the lower of (Essence times) or (double Strength). Bonus Decisive damage. May pay with Initiative instead of motes.<br /> DB: Strength of Stone Technique. Simple. 5m, +1 Strength/scene. Must be standing on the ground. Bonus Withering damage.<br /> <br /> The bonus damage is a wash. The DB Charm is more expensive (to the point of raising your Anima), not stackable, and has conditions on its use. Honestly there's not much in it. You are usually standing on the ground. +2m isn't a massive deal. You are really unlikey to be in a position where you can just stand still and charge up Increasing Strength Exercise five times in a row. But the Solar Charm is clearly better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the solar charm needs to (or can) charge up 5 rounds in a row. By my reading, you can increase your strength by up to the cap with a single activation, with the mote/initiative cost scaling to the strength increase.<br /> I also think the Solar and Dragonblooded charms increase withering damage by the same amount - the I read the dragonblooded mention of increasing withering damage as clarifying what increasing strength does, not on top of increasing strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T19:32:41-07:00","id":1380273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1380151#post1380151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an Essence 3 Solar Investigation Charm which gives you 3 <i>Charm</i> successes for 6m. Basically giving you a Muted, no discount Excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually [your Essence] successes, for 6m. Not especially a good bargain if you picked it up at Essence 1 via Supernal, but at the same time, it's also <i>scene-length</i>, making it potentially useful in a scene where one must profile a number of people at once, or have to do a Case Scene <i>and</i> Profile some characters. Like, say, a murder at a dinner party?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1380151#post1380151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also have Shadow Over Day, which is &quot;buy a Charm to save 1m under extremely limited circumstances... maybe&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very uncharitable reading of the Charm. Shadow Over Day is cheaper for raising your Guile than just using an Excellency, <i>and</i> has the Mute Keyword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-11-2020, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T01:18:47-07:00","id":1380336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1380273#post1380273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very uncharitable reading of the Charm. Shadow Over Day is cheaper for raising your Guile than just using an Excellency, <i>and</i> has the Mute Keyword.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you've used the Charm and I haven't, I will bow to your experience here.<br /> <br /> But my reading of SoD is that it is the worst, weakest Charm in the history of Exalted. The Dragon-Blooded Socailize Excellency is Mute. The Dragon-Blooded equivalent Charm (Smoke-Wreathed Mien) is a cap-breaker boost to Guile.<br /> <br /> Personas look fun, and Mute Charms are a bigger deal for Solars than DBs (depending on where your game is set, Guile is arguably a bigger deal for Solars than Deebs). So... I trust your opinion and guess it's more useful than it looks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-11-2020, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:02:14-07:00","id":1380406,"title":"","content":"Shadow Over Day is one of those Charms that don't look like much at a first glance, but then turn out to be ridiculously useful in actual play.<br /> <br /> - it allows basically any character to max out their Guile without having to spend peripheral motes or flare their anima<br /> - after an extended social scene, it can trivially leave you with 10+ extra motes in the tank (especially from E2 on)<br /> - at E2, it allows you to counter the effects of a 4m expenditure (which, for Dragon-Blooded, is a full excellency for anybody who is not invested in reading intentions to the max, and for Celestials, often the practical limit of what they can toss around more than once in a scene) for half the cost<br /> <br /> Any Solar who cares about keeping their cards close to their chest does themselves a massive disservice by skipping this Charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:15:21-07:00","id":1380412,"title":"","content":"Plus if you pick up Preeminent Gala Knife then it's practically free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T03:00:03-07:00","id":1381580,"title":"","content":"DB charms are generally either more expensive, more limited, or just weaker. In general if a Solar charm does X, then a DB charm will:<br /> A) Do X but cost a WP when the solar charm didn't.<br /> B) Do X but only against Fair Folk, or Demons, or some other relatively narrow specilaization.<br /> C) Do 2/3rds of X.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T00:07:10-07:00","id":1403952,"title":"","content":"they are about half as powerful as a solar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25272-cypheriel","name":"Cypheriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T07:59:28-07:00","id":1404402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1380336#post1380336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But my reading of Unimpeachable Discourse Technique is that it is the worst, weakest Charm in the history of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>FTFY, you were <i>one</i> page off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T09:23:21-07:00","id":1404418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1404402#post1404402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FTFY, you were <i>one</i> page off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As a person with Unimpeachable Discourse Technique, I must admit that I've never used it, and would have vastly preferred if Aspersions Cast Aside had been in its place on the tree... but I still don't think it's the worst one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T09:23:39-07:00","id":1404419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1404402#post1404402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> FTFY, you were <i>one</i> page off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>5 Attribute 5 Ability 1 Specialty 2 Stunt 10 Excellency<br /> <br /> You're rolling 23 dice. 3m for 2 non-Charm dice isn't terrible. Add in dice tricks (like double 9s from Impassioned Orator Technique) and it becomes genuinely good.<br /> <br /> The problem comes when you add in the restrictions on when you can use the Charm, the fact that you're never going to be hitting a Resolve higher than 10 (and likely not higher than 4) and the lack of anti-Solar magic relying on rolled 1s... and then Unimpeachable Discourse Technique becomes pretty terrible, pretty quickly.<br /> <br /> It should, at least, also be usable on Inspire rolls and be Mute. Which would make it merely a &quot;bad&quot; Charm. But as written it's not the worst charm ever. Bottom 10 maybe, but not the worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T17:50:48-07:00","id":1404489,"title":"","content":"Solars rerolling 1s for 3m is an Essence 1 Charm that also gives an automatic success and sometimes only costs 2m. Except Socialize which for some reason only gets the reroll and not until Essence 2 and only under hyperspecific circumstances. There\u2019s nothing about that that isn\u2019t the worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T02:28:08-07:00","id":1404556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1404489#post1404489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solars rerolling 1s for 3m is an Essence 1 Charm that also gives an automatic success and sometimes only costs 2m. Except Socialize which for some reason only gets the reroll and not until Essence 2 and only under hyperspecific circumstances. There\u2019s nothing about that that isn\u2019t the worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different abilities are different. The power of Rerolling 1s depends massively on what other dicetricks can be brought to bear, and what the typical difficulties and concequences of failure are. <br /> <br /> I do agree that it should probably be Essence 1 though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T05:06:27-07:00","id":1404571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1380336#post1380336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But my reading of SoD is that it is the worst, weakest Charm in the history of Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>When we're in a Dragon-Blooded charm thread I feel obligated to remind people that Manual of Exalted Power: Dragon-Blooded was a real thing.<br /> <br /> What's that 2e Talented Improvisation? You let people play a musical instrument without penalty even if they lack a specialty? Oh my, how generous!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T05:16:42-07:00","id":1404572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1404571#post1404571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When we're in a Dragon-Blooded charm thread I feel obligated to remind people that Manual of Exalted Power: Dragon-Blooded was a real thing.<br /> <br /> What's that 2e Talented Improvisation? You let people play a musical instrument without penalty even if they lack a specialty? Oh my, how generous!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm glad they didn't slip in a clause about it failing to work on magical instruments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T02:36:27-07:00","id":1404733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1380094-how-good-are-db-charms?p=1404571#post1404571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When we're in a Dragon-Blooded charm thread I feel obligated to remind people that Manual of Exalted Power: Dragon-Blooded was a real thing.<br /> <br /> What's that 2e Talented Improvisation? You let people play a musical instrument without penalty even if they lack a specialty? Oh my, how generous!</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair comment. But at least it got <a href=\"https://www.dictionary.com/browse/errata\" target=\"_blank\">errata</a>.<br /> <br /> Older editions weren't perfect, but they didn't profess to be. The game got patched. Errors were made, were named specifically as errors, then rectified.<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you know the difference between an error and a mistake, Ensign?&quot; <br /> 'No, sir.' <br /> &quot;Anyone can make an error, Ensign. But that error doesn't become a mistake until you refuse to correct it.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3E has been of far higher quality than 2E. Far higher. And Minton and Vance have done a great job both with their published works and interactions with the community.<br /> <br /> But 2E's paradigm was to spit out a truckload of books at 70% quality then patch them upto 90%. 3E's paradigm seems to be to labour each book upto 90% and never touch them again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T04:19:30-07:00","id":1404748,"title":"","content":"Second Edition didn't meaningfully attempt to fix things until after Return of the Scarlet Empress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T12:29:07-07:00","id":1405979,"title":"","content":"The thing about Errata is that it\u2019s given for free to the community and thus usually unpaid labor. I\u2019d much rather have the authors paid to get a book up to 90% than not.<br /> <br /> And, in a lot of cases, you can\u2019t really find the problems without letting a large community stress test stuff for several years, so clearing that final 10% is difficult on any kind of realistic timescale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}